ssage(s) returned by the walker (if pre‑walk was true) are still added to the result set before the exception', 'description': 'When the post‑walk listener throws, the exception should not be swallowed; it must be re‑thrown after the finally block finishes. Messages collected before the exception must still be present in the returned set (if the method returns before the exception is thrown, the test can verify the exception is thrown).'}]}, {'group': 'Null executionContext – listeners receive null without NPE', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': None}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'mockNode'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'mockRootNode'}, {'parameter': 'at', 'value': '"/null‑ctx"'}, {'parameter': 'shouldValidateSchema', 'value': 'true'}], 'expected': 'walk proceeds; pre‑walk and post‑walk listeners are invoked with a null executionContext; no NullPointerException is thrown', 'description': 'The method should not assume executionContext is non‑null; it must forward the null value to listeners and walkers, allowing them to handle it.'}]}, {'group': 'shouldValidateSchema = false – walker still invoked', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mockExecutionContext'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'mockNode'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'mockRootNode'}, {'parameter': 'at', 'value': '"/no‑validate"'}, {'parameter': 'shouldValidateSchema', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'validationMessages contains the messages returned by the walker (e.g., "msg‑from‑walker"), proving that the flag does not prevent walker execution; post‑walk listener is still called', 'description': 'The boolean flag is only passed to the walker; the walk method itself does not branch on it. This test confirms that setting it to false does not skip the walker.'}]}]
